guide forever/professions/cooking
title Cooking 1-300
category Professions
coords era
levels 5-60
zone Ironforge

# Cooking 1-300 for both factions: recipes in orange/yellow order from
# professions.json. Trainer recipes up to 130 (Forever teaches Coyote Steak,
# Boiled Clams, Crab Cake and Dry Pork Ribs well below their yellow rank: the
# sniffed trainer lists), then vendor recipes whose ingredients drop far more
# often than the trainer's clams and spider meat (Curiously Tasty Omelet, Hot
# Lion Chops, Roast Raptor). Each segment says where its ingredients drop (the
# densest cluster of normal creatures that drop them, or the clams that hold
# them, from items.json) or the vendor that sells them. Expert is a cookbook
# (Shandrina, Ashenvale / Wulan, Desolace); Artisan is the Clamlette Surprise
# quest in Gadgetzan. Poached Sunscale Salmon, the usual Classic finish, needs
# an Iron Oven on Forever (the skill-300 camp feature): the route ends on
# Monster Omelet.
# Craft counts use the Classic skill-up chance (grey - skill) / (grey - yellow).
# INGAME: can a character under level 20 read the Expert Cookbook at skill 125?
# (the book carries no level requirement; Classic guides gate it at 20)
#
# Spawns come from the reference data: the Era baseline (pfQuest) plus the
# node spawns Forever's beta sniffs add (Zephras Isle, the starting-area Poor
# Copper Veins and herbs: the Forever TrinityCore world DB); trainer learn skills
# and prices from Forever's sniffed trainer lists; recipes and their skill colours
# from the Forever client tables (`forge data professions`).
# ASSUMED: past level 30 (the beta's cap) Forever's spawns are Classic's; nothing
# confirms them yet. In-game check: refine with Polestar_Recorder sessions.
# ASSUMED: rank level gates are Classic's (Journeyman 10, Expert 20, Artisan 35);
# Forever's sniffed trainer lists show none (the gate sits on the rank spell, a
# table we lack); only Journeyman Fishing is sniffed at level 10. In-game check:
# the level a trainer asks for each rank.
# Waypoints are Era-frame (`coords era`); the engine converts them where Forever
# changed a map frame, and a map without an Era frame (Zephras Isle) compiles live.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice
section Cooking 1-50

step Learn Cooking
  tip Any Cooking trainer of your faction teaches Apprentice Cooking (character level 5, 1s); the arrow picks the nearest. Forever: every cook knows Basic Campfire. Craft a Basic Campfire Kit from one Simple Wood (38c) with Flint and Tinder (1s 35c, kept in your bags), then place the kit to light a cooking fire anywhere; make a few in advance (one use every 5 minutes). The first kits also raise Cooking to about 5. The Camping 101: Cooking quest at your starting area's camp sends you to this trainer.
  level 5
  train Cooking Apprentice

